<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aspavarma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aspavarma was a ruler of the Apracharajas, a dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bajaur">Bajaur</a> in the north-west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</a>, in the early 1st century CE. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indravarma">Indravarma</a>, he is known from coins on which he calls himself <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strategos">strategos</a>, a general, serving first under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indo-scythians">Indo-Scythian</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azes-i">Azes</a> and then under the Indo-Parthian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gondophares">Gondophares</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aspavarma.jpg" alt="Aspavarma" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apracharajas_Aspavarama.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
